['Linked-list cycle detection','Detect a cycle in a singly linked list with O(1) extra space. Why do slow and fast pointers meet?','Floyd algorithm بيحرّك slow خطوة وfast خطوتين. لو فيه cycle، فرق مواقعهم جوه الدورة بيتغير لحد ما يتقابلوا؛ لو fast وصل null مفيش cycle.','Advance slow by one and fast by two while fast and its next node exist. Compare node identity, not stored value; a meeting implies a cycle. Time O(n), space O(1). Test empty lists, self-loops and repeated values without a cycle; avoid dereferencing null.','two speeds~slow/fast|node identity~identity/===|null termination~null|complexity~o(n)/o(1)','تساوي values بتاعة nodeين مش معناه إنهم نفس node أو فيه cycle.']
